548 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 139 0 R
/T (In this run the time of += grew almost linearly with n, not quadratically. This is the CPython optimisation mentioned above: when the left-hand string has exactly one reference, the interpreter extends it in place with a realloc, so most iterations do not copy the whole text. To confirm that thequadratic behaviour is real, the supplementary experiment keeps a second reference \(keep = text\) beforeeach +=. The reference count becomestwo, the in-place shortcut is not allowed, and every addition copies thewhole string. )
/E (In this run the time of += grew almost linearly with n, not quadratically. This is the CPython optimisation mentioned above: when the left-hand string has exactly one reference, the interpreter extends it in place with a realloc, so most iterations do not copy the whole text. To confirm that thequadratic behaviour is real, the supplementary experiment keeps a second reference \(keep = text\) beforeeach +=. The reference count becomestwo, the in-place shortcut is not allowed, and every addition copies thewhole string. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
