/Title (Conclusion: while recursion is useful for traversing trees, for a simple linear recurrence like this one the iterative approach is superior because it avoids the heavy overhead of the call stack and the risk of stack overflow. The original version is preferable only for very small n, where brevity matters more than performance.)
