/Title (In this run the time of += grew almost linearly with n, not quadratically. This is the CPython optimisation mentioned above: when the left-hand string has exactly one reference, the interpreter extends it in place with a realloc, so most iterations do not copy the whole text. To confirm that thequadratic behaviour is real, the supplementary experiment keeps a second reference \(keep = text\) beforeeach +=. The reference count becomestwo, the in-place shortcut is not allowed, and every addition copies thewhole string.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2119 0 R
