/Title (Strings in Python are immutable: once a string object is created in memory, its content cannot be changed. When we perform an operation like text.upper\(\), Python does not modify the original text variable; instead it creates a brand-new string object in a different memory location with the upper-case characters and)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2155 0 R
/Next 2176 0 R
>>
endobj
2176 0 obj
<<
/Title (returns it. This is why calling text.upper\(\) without assigning the result back \(for example text text.upper\(\)\) produces no visible change in the original variable.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2155 0 R
/Prev 2175 0 R
>>
endobj
